    "q-42704": {
      "dom_id": "step-q42704",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,N=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrices $M$, $N$ and $P$ are not elementary matrices because they can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.",
