    "q-130788": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130788",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Find the inverse of the elementary matrix \n$N=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "We write down $N$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[N\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{12} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:=12{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{N}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
